2026-09-27T09:45:52.7560055Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7560224Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7560458Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7560681Z 
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7560759Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7560934Z ================
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7561037Z 
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7561157Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7561449Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7561807Z 
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7561938Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7562267Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7562471Z 
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7562637Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7563007Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7563298Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7563791Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7564178Z 
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7564276Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7564623Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7565040Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7565250Z 
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7565493Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7565792Z 
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7565874Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7627635Z ========
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7627952Z 
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7629052Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7630167Z 
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7630385Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7630764Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7631500Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7632243Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7632680Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7633013Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7633390Z 
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7633487Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7633714Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7633826Z 
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7634596Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7635431Z 
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7635901Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7636556Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:45:52.7636721Z 
